LarpOS - Blood Moon (Arch Linux based live system)

  Quick start:
    - Desktop autologins as "liveuser" (KDE Plasma, Blood Moon theme)
    - Open a terminal and run "sudo archinstall" to install to disk
    - "larp-info" shows system info with the LarpOS mask
    - Internet: NetworkManager - use the network icon in the system tray
      or "nmtui" in a terminal

  Packages are managed with pacman. AUR helpers (yay, paru) can be
  installed after installing the system to disk.

  LarpOS is an independent distribution based on Arch Linux.
  It is not affiliated with or endorsed by Arch Linux or Mr. Robot.
